# SINGLE-OWNER SUB-PLACE NEG — the by-design carve-out at a FIELD place.
# `Callable[T]` has no implicit-copy path in the lowering, so a bare `h.f` read
# binds a SECOND owner of one closure env. Two plain `h.f` reads are an
# `AddressSanitizer: attempting double-free`; a re-read across a scope is a
# heap-use-after-free — both at `gg check` rc 0 before the gate was widened.
#
# The gate keys on the OUTERMOST PROJECTION (the ratified PLACE/TEMP axis,
# decisions.md D31 ADDENDUM 2026-07-20). Bare INDEX places (`v[0]`, `d[k]`) are
# the NAMED OMITTED CELL: equally unsound today (todo/t1225), deferred behind
# the owner's callee-borrow ruling (2026-09-04 — a call does not consume its
# callee) rather than shipping a per-request clone on the httpserver hot path.
# A read THROUGH a container (`v[0].f`) IS in scope — see the sibling cell.
#
# CELL: type=Callable · place=field of a LOCAL · position=bind · capture=int.
# RED at 7bf11017e: `gg check` ACCEPTED (rc 0).
# ggdef: ABSTAIN — its arm keys on a bare identifier of `Ty::Callable`; the
# sub-place reach is out of subset (todo/t1227).

struct Holder:
    Callable[int()] f

Callable[int()] mk(int n):
    return (): n + 1

void main():
    Holder h = Holder(mk(40))
    Callable[int()] g = h.f
    print(g())
